Implemented and locally verified the Track B generator for the [paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/2506.12019).

- [Generator](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.12019/gen_2506_12019.py)
- [Self-test report](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.12019/selftest_report.json)
- [README](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.12019/README.md)
- [Bare transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.12019/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [Hinted transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.12019/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [Placebo transcript](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/2506.12019/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Local results:

- All G1–G9(c) gates pass.
- Legal candidate space: 847,660,528.
- Random guessing: 0/250,000.
- Four attacks: each 0/8.
- Meet-in-the-middle reference: 8/8, averaging 1,167,727 states and 5,468,684 operations.
- Compact route: verified, 185-operation bound.
- Answer remains ten IDs when `n` doubles.
- Exhaustive fuzzing confirmed uniqueness across small parameter ranges.

The result is not yet shippable: all three oracle runs were attempted, but OpenRouter returned HTTP 403 `Key limit exceeded (total limit)` before any model produced a scored attempt. The script-owned error transcripts were retained; no false hardness verdict was claimed. Restoring the OpenRouter quota and rerunning `harden.py` is the only remaining step.
